"l2753 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l2753.pdf)\nciteturn1462view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":322}); Total lines: 34\nL0@P0: ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF CONFIDENTIALITY\nL1@P0: EARLY NEUTRAL EVALUATION (ENE) SESSION\nL2@P0: Adopted for Mandatory Use\nL3@P0: L2753 (New February 2008)\nL4@P0: ADR NEUTRAL NAME, ADDRESS, TELEPHONE, FAX AND EMAIL:\nL5@P0: PLAINTIFF/PETITIONER:\nL6@P0: DEFENDANT/RESPONDENT:\nL7@P0: ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF CONFIDENTIALITY\nL8@P0: EARLY NEUTRAL EVALUATION (ENE) SESSION\nL9@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL10@P0: (DO NOT FILE WITH THE COURT)\nL11@P0: This form is provided to offer ADR Neutrals as a convenient means to inform participants of the applicable ethical and other rules.\nL12@P0: The participants in the ENE proceeding of this case agree that:\nL13@P0: 1. No written or oral communication made by any party, attorney, neutral, or other participant in preparation for or in\nL14@P0: any ENE session in this case may be used for any purpose in any pending or future proceeding unless all parties,\nL15@P0: including the neutral, so agree. This prohibition specifically applies to any written evaluation prepared by the\nL16@P0: neutral in the course of the ENE session. Disclosure of information that otherwise is privileged will not alter its\nL17@P0: privileged character.\nL18@P0: 2. The parties will not subpoena the neutral or any documents submitted to or prepared by the neutral during or in\nL19@P0: connection with the ENE process. The neutral will not testify voluntarily on behalf of a party.\nL20@P0: 3. This agreement will not preclude a report of information to the ADR Administrator or an inquiry by the\nL21@P0: Administrator regarding complaints against a neutral.\nL22@P0: 4. This agreement does not affect the admissibility of a written settlement agreement reached as a result of this ENE\nL23@P0: proceeding in an action to enforce that settlement.\nL24@P0: Dated:\nL25@P0: Neutral\nL26@P0: Party Party\nL27@P0: Attorney Attorney\nL28@P0: Party Party\nL29@P0: Attorney Attorney\nL30@P0: Other Participant Other Participant\nL31@P0: Title Title\nL32@P0: Representing (specify party) Representing (specify party)\nL33@P0:  Additional pages attached (number) _______\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nl2754 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l2754.pdf)\nciteturn1462view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":323}); Total lines: 36\nL0@P0: ADR NEUTRAL NAME, ADDRESS, TELEPHONE, FAX AND EMAIL:\nL1@P0: PLAINTIFF/PETITIONER:\nL2@P0: DEFENDANT/RESPONDENT:\nL3@P0: ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF CONFIDENTIALITY\nL4@P0: MEDIATION SESSION\nL5@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL6@P0: (DO NOT FILE WITH THE COURT)\nL7@P0: This form is provided to offer mediators a convenient means to inform participants of the applicable ethical and other rules.\nL8@P0: The participants in the mediation proceeding of this case agree that:\nL9@P0: 1. The mediation proceeding will be confidential, in accordance with California Evidence Code sections 703.5 and\nL10@P0: 1115 through 1128.\nL11@P0: 2. This agreement does not affect the admissibility of a written settlement agreement reached as a result of this\nL12@P0: mediation proceeding in an action to enforce that settlement.\nL13@P0: 3. This agreement will not preclude a report of information to the ADR Administrator or an inquiry by the\nL14@P0: Administrator regarding complaints against a neutral pursuant to California Rules of Court, rules 3.850 through\nL15@P0: 3.863.\nL16@P0: Dated:___________________________ ____________________________________________________\nL17@P0: Neutral\nL18@P0: _______________________________________________________ ____________________________________________________\nL19@P0: Party Party\nL20@P0: __________________________________________